Why: one state folder for the driver's own config (CUA_DRIVER_STATE_DIR), so an embedding app keeps it beside its other state instead of ~/.cua-driver.

When CUA_DRIVER_STATE_DIR is set and not empty, every reader and writer of the
driver's config.json uses <CUA_DRIVER_STATE_DIR>/config.json: the macOS config
(set_config/get_config and startup load), the preview-window config, the
cursor motion defaults and the run_script switch. Unset, nothing changes.
Other state already has its own override (CUA_DRIVER_CURSOR_THEME_DIR,
CUA_DRIVER_BROWSER_PROFILE_ROOT); paths the caller passes with ~ still mean the
user's home. Upstreamable as is.

